het.","extract_html":"<p><b>Gününa Küne</b> (Puelche) is an extinct Chonan language formerly spoken by the Gününa Küne people in the Pampas region of Argentina. The language is also known as Gennaken (Guenaken), Northern Tehuelche, <i>Gününa Yajüch</i>, Ranquelche, Septentrional Austral Tehuelche and Pampa. It was also spoken by the Chechehet.</p>"}